---
// src/pages/about.astro - About page
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';

---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Jake Maisel - Senior Product Designer"
  description="11 years of professional design experience with 5+ years in UX/product design. Specializing in strategic product rationalization, mobile-first design, and research-led decision making in automotive marketplaces.">
  <section class="about-page">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <div class="page-hero-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">About · Senior Product Designer</p>
        <h1>I design for the people who keep the <em>whole operation</em> running.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Dealers, accountants, back-office teams: I make high-stakes work faster, clearer, and easier to verify.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <section class="about-content">
        <div class="intro-section">
          <p class="intro-text">
            I design and ship products that matter. With 11 years of professional design experience and 5+ years specializing in UX and product design, I've led cross-functional teams to solve complex problems through rigorous research and clear communication. My work at ACV Auctions and across automotive marketplaces has shaped how I approach product strategy, user research, and organizational alignment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="expertise-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">What I Do</h2>
          <div class="expertise-list">
            <div class="expertise-item">
              <dt class="expertise-title">Product Rationalization</dt>
              <dd class="expertise-description">
                Audit portfolios, eliminate redundancy, and design consolidation strategies that free capacity.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="expertise-item">
              <dt class="expertise-title">Mobile-First Design</dt>
              <dd class="expertise-description">
                Redesign for context, not just scale: Market Report on the lot, ClearCar's dealer portal, and MAX on mobile.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="expertise-item">
              <dt class="expertise-title">AI Integration</dt>
              <dd class="expertise-description">
                Put AI where it earns trust: AI damage detection in ClearCar's offers, and AI-assisted workflows for my own design team.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="expertise-item">
              <dt class="expertise-title">Research-Led Design</dt>
              <dd class="expertise-description">
                Use rigorous research to uncover problems others miss and back solutions with data.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="expertise-item">
              <dt class="expertise-title">Cross-Functional Leadership</dt>
              <dd class="expertise-description">
                Own strategy to execution, connecting teams with competing incentives toward shared goals.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="lead-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the screen</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">How I <em class="grad-text">lead</em>.</h2>
          <p class="lead-intro">
            The best design work I've done keeps paying off after I've moved on, because it changed how the team works, not just what it shipped.
          </p>
          <div class="lead-grid">
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">01</span>
              <h3>Set the team's operating rules</h3>
              <p>I co-owned how ACV Retail plans and hands off work: plan the big picture first, one ticket per deliverable, and no blocker sits for more than two business days. Then I modeled it, with every handoff including the prototype, acceptance criteria, every state, and accessibility notes.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">02</span>
              <h3>Build systems others reuse</h3>
              <p>I led the white-label component work behind Guaranteed Sale: audits, three standardization workshops with design and engineering, written guidelines, and the component build. Designs estimated at 20+ weeks took under 10.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">03</span>
              <h3>Design in code</h3>
              <p>For ClearCar's 2026 customer offer widget, the design lived in a live Storybook prototype, not static mockups. I joined engineering code review and fixed real bugs before handoff.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">04</span>
              <h3>Put AI to work, carefully</h3>
              <p>I wrote ACV's playbook for using Claude to create in-product guides: templates, tone rules, and sequencing, so any designer can draft guides and prototypes quickly while staying consistent.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">05</span>
              <h3>Measure what ships</h3>
              <p>For MAX's mobile "Take Into Inventory" flow, I built tracking into the handoff so the team could see starts, completions, and errors from day one. It launched with zero critical issues.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="lead-item edge-card">
              <span class="lead-num">06</span>
              <h3>Share what I learn</h3>
              <p>Weekly UX updates for ACV Retail, an onboarding deck for new partners, a Tech Talk for non-designers on dealer negotiation, and presentations at ACV's Research &amp; Design Journal.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="philosophy-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">How I Work</h2>

          <div class="philosophy-list">
            <div class="philosophy-item">
              <h3>Discover</h3>
              <p>
                Every project begins with understanding. I talk to users, map their jobs to be done, identify workflows, and separate signal from noise. This prevents addressing the wrong problem—which is worse than solving the right problem poorly.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="philosophy-item">
              <h3>Define</h3>
              <p>
                Once I've diverged and explored, I narrow. Constraints force prioritization and eliminate the unnecessary. I devote substantial effort to stakeholder communication, ensuring alignment before exploring solutions. Great design fails without alignment.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="philosophy-item">
              <h3>Develop</h3>
              <p>
                With the problem clearly defined, I explore solutions. Every major decision is backed by research, metrics, or prototyping. I generate multiple directions, test them, and let data guide which to pursue.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="philosophy-item">
              <h3>Deliver</h3>
              <p>
                Success isn't measured by deliverables shipped. It's measured by whether the solution moved key metrics, achieved user adoption, and generated learning for future initiatives. I refine until the work produces real business impact.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="background-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Background</h2>
          <p>
            Throughout my career, I've focused on the automotive marketplace where product complexity mirrors real-world business challenges. At ACV Auctions and other marketplaces, I've tackled problems at scale—consolidating redundant product lines, unlocking AI capabilities, scaling systems from zero to millions in transactions, and bridging the gap between dealer needs and platform capabilities.
          </p>
          <p>
            I'm particularly drawn to cross-platform problems where the right answer requires deep research, systems-level thinking, and cross-functional coordination. I work best in environments where constraints force clarity and where design decisions are grounded in data rather than opinion. My approach combines strategic product thinking with hands-on design execution, ensuring that insights translate into user impact and business outcomes.
          </p>
        </section>
      </section>
    </div>

    <ContactCTA />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  .about-content {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .intro-section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-title {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .expertise-section,
  .lead-section,
  .philosophy-section,
  .background-section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .lead-section .section-title {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .lead-intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .lead-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lead-item {
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .lead-num {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: var(--gradient);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
    width: fit-content;
  }

  .lead-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .lead-item p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .expertise-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .expertise-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .expertise-item:hover {
    border-color: var(--gradient-start);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(var(--brand-teal-rgb), 0.1);
  }

  .expertise-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .expertise-description {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .philosophy-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .philosophy-item {
    padding: 0;
  }

  .philosophy-item h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .philosophy-item p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .background-section p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .background-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .lead-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .container {
      padding: 0 1rem;
    }

    .about-content {
      padding: 2rem 0;
    }

    .expertise-list,
    .lead-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .philosophy-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

  }
</style>
